LibreChat batch 1 (#125): the newly enabled search, side-by-side compare and context gauge, made right for Arabic.
Behaviour that CSS and the Arabic overlay cannot change:
- the search box mirrors in RTL: the icon at the start (right), the clear button at the end (left), and the text padded
  on both sides, so the button no longer covers the first letters of the query (desktop and phone);
- the bar of a model added for side-by-side compare names the picked spec («+ بصير لايت»), not the label of its
  endpoint («+ بصير», shared by two specs), and its remove button has a translated name (com_efaiw_remove_added_model)
  instead of the hard-coded "Close added conversation";
- the context gauge uses Western digits in every language, like the dates (#120).

